|}

A vector passes if its script, run on its witness under the witness script rules, gives the stated result. The result MUST be the same with and without the standard policy flags.

Vector 2 is the first depth at which the leaf index takes two bytes. Vector 3 is a stateless signature in the form a block signer provides it, with no SIGHASH byte. Vector 1 is also written out below.

